<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#customs-union">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Customs union</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A customs union is an agreement among territories to remove tariffs between them and adopt a common external tariff. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> formed a single customs union covering about fifty million people for fifty years. Its dissolution after 1918 severed economic links and caused prolonged disruption in the successor states.</p></div>
